Wait — my dedupe in newPulseSamples uses `fresh[fresh.length-1].tUs` while iterating, so it only skips if the *previous kept* is >= current. But if unordered: [4s, 3s] → kept 4s, then 3s <= 4s → skipped! That defeats the purpose.

I need: collect all readings above the floor, then sort, then dedupe. Let me fix:

```ts
const collected: PulseSample[] = [];
for (const raw of series) { const s = toPulseSample(raw, anchor, lastTUs); if (s) collected.push(s); }
collected.sort((a,b) => a.tUs - b.tUs);
const fresh: PulseSample[] = [];
for (const sample of collected) {
  if (fresh.length > 0 && sample.tUs === fresh[fresh.length-1].tUs) continue; // keep first (stable sort keeps payload order)
  fresh.push(sample);
}
```
Array.prototype.sort is stable in modern V8, so duplicates keep payload order → first kept. Matches the test expectation.

